    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24976" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrĭgātĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inr-</span></b> ),
			ōnis, f.
		irrigo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a watering</i>, <i>irrigating</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quos (pulvinos) irrigationes abluunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 35, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agrorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 2, 4, 14</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">agri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. de Sen. 15, 53</span></i>
			.— With <i>gen. subj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrigatione fluminis diluere aliquid,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					36, 12, 17, § 81</span></i>
			.—Also transf., <i>refreshment</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">irrigation ossium tuorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Prov. 3, 8</span></i>
			.</div>
